    "result_text": "Done. The full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 2/2 tests passing, including both new `ownerSegment` acceptance tests).\n\n## What I changed\n\nThree small, cohesive edits following the existing derived-field pattern:\n\n1. **New standalone unit** `OwnerSegment.java` \u2014 a single static `of(Owner)` method (CC \u2248 4, no surrounding class context to hold). It reads the same `customerCode` prefix used by `locality`/`OwnerTimezone` to get the region, maps `membershipLevel \u2265 3 \u2192 PREMIUM` else `STANDARD`, and `{NSW,VIC,QLD} \u2192 METRO` else `REGIONAL`.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 one added `@Mapping` line delegating to `OwnerSegment.of(owner)`. The mapper interface has no method bodies, so its WMC_other is trivial.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `ownerSegment` schema property so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field.\n\n## Why this keeps structural impact low\n\nThe core logic lives in a brand-new class where `WMC_other = 0` (only the private constructor), so `cost = max(0,1) * CC * changed_lines` stays minimal rather than paying for a large surrounding class. The only edit to existing code is a one-line annotation on a body-less mapper interface method \u2014 again near-zero surrounding complexity. No existing method was grown and no large class was touched, which keeps the file-count multiplier working against the smallest possible per-function costs.\n\nThe derivation correctly matches the tests: `knownOwner(\"Sydney\")` \u2192 postcode 2000 \u2192 `NSW-\u2026` customerCode \u2192 `STANDARD_METRO`; random-city owner \u2192 `UNKNOWN-\u2026` \u2192 `STANDARD_REGIONAL`.",
